## 4. API (add to Section 35)

All routes are under `/api/v1`, JWT-protected, and filtered by `userId` from the token.

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/documents/:docId/annotations?since=ISO` | List (incremental sync with `since`) |
| POST | `/documents/:docId/annotations` | Create (client-generated `id`) |
| PATCH | `/annotations/:id` | Update marks / note / pinned |
| DELETE | `/annotations/:id` | Soft delete (sets `deletedAt`) |
| GET/POST/DELETE | `/documents/:docId/bookmarks` | Bookmarks |
| PUT | `/sessions/:docId/progress` | **Existing** — extend body with `anchor`, `percent`, `deviceId` |
| GET | `/lookup?term=&lang=en` | Dictionary + Wikipedia summary, cached in Redis (7 days) |
| POST | `/documents/:docId/reports` | Report extraction error |
| GET | `/documents/:docId/outline` | Chapters/headings tree with `startOffset`, `level`, `title`, `totalChars` |

**Sync rule [A]:** last-write-wins on `updatedAt`; deletes are tombstones. The client keeps an IndexedDB queue (`offlineQueue.ts`) and replays it when online. Reading position syncs at most every 5 s and on page turn debounce.

