### F3 — Running header and footer

**Observed [V]:** a small grey running header with the book title on each page; footer-left "**5 min left in chapter**" (also "**24 mins left in book**"); footer-right "**11 %**".

**Build [A]**

```ts
// progress.ts
const MIN_WPM = 80, MAX_WPM = 600, DEFAULT_WPM = 200;
export class ReadingSpeed {
  private wpm = DEFAULT_WPM;
  recordTurn(wordsOnView: number, seconds: number) {
    if (seconds < 3 || seconds > 180) return;       // ignore skims and idle time
    const sample = Math.min(MAX_WPM, Math.max(MIN_WPM, wordsOnView / (seconds / 60)));
    this.wpm = 0.9 * this.wpm + 0.1 * sample;       // exponential moving average
  }
  minutesLeft(wordsRemaining: number) { return Math.max(1, Math.round(wordsRemaining / this.wpm)); }
}
```

Format as "N min left in chapter" / "N mins left in book" (singular/plural). Footer-left cycles *chapter → book → page → none* when tapped; this cycle is **[A]**, and the Reading Progress setting (F11) chooses the default. Persist `wpm` per user.

