### F5 — Scrubber, previews and the "Back to N" chip

**Observed [V]:** dragging the slider shows a filmstrip of **three page previews** (previous / current / next) with bookmark ribbons, and the label updates live. After a jump, a small floating **thumbnail labelled "Back to 17" / "Back to 60"** appears at the bottom-right and stays while you browse (≈0:04–1:58).

**Build**

```ts
// jumpStack.ts — return-to-place after non-sequential jumps
export class JumpStack {
  private stack: Anchor[] = [];
  push(a: Anchor) { if (!this.stack.length || far(this.stack.at(-1)!, a)) this.stack.push(a); }
  pop(): Anchor | undefined { return this.stack.pop(); }
  peek(): Anchor | undefined { return this.stack.at(-1); }
  clear() { this.stack = []; }
}
// push the CURRENT position before: scrubber commit, TOC jump, search result, internal link, grid pick
```

- Scrubber ratio → offset: `offset = round(ratio · totalChars)`; ticks at `chapter.startOffset / totalChars`.
- Previews: render three miniature clones of the chapter flow (scaled ≈ 0.3) translated to views *v−1, v, v+1*. Cache by `(chapterId, view, settingsHash)`; only build while the thumb is down. For very long chapters, throttle to 10 updates/s.
- The chip: shows a thumbnail of the saved position; tap → `goTo(stack.pop())`. **[A]** It disappears when tapped, when you have read on > 10 views past the jump target, or when the book closes.

