## 8. Accessibility, performance, offline

- **Accessibility:** toolbar and sheets are real `<button>`s with labels; sheets are focus-trapped; the image viewer uses `<dialog>`; announce page changes through an `aria-live="polite"` region ("Page 18 of 62"); every swatch has a name (as in the video); contrast of the four page colours ≥ 4.5:1; full keyboard map (arrows, `b` bookmark, `/` search, `t` contents).
- **Reduce motion:** disable the curl and slide animations when `prefers-reduced-motion` is set.
- **Performance:** render one chapter; limit overlay repaint to the visible views; use `content-visibility: auto` for off-screen chapters; throttle scrubber previews; cache previews and `charsPerPage`; keep `getClientRects` calls batched (read all, then write all).
- **Offline:** cache chapter text + annotations in IndexedDB (service worker caches the app shell); queue annotation writes; show a small "offline" badge. AI features (lookup, explain) are online-only.
- **Privacy:** annotations and notes are private to the user; deleting a document deletes its annotations, bookmarks and reports.

